{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions","id":1543830,"title":"On the premise of how Presence functions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-14T21:45:14-07:00","id":1543830,"title":"On the premise of how Presence functions","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> So, this is a hot topic, somewhat. At least in every table I've been STing since I was a kid. How should we consider many of the functions of Presence to work, Presence is a discipline that's always bound to create some discussion about its funcioning, because on one hand anyone can resist it with a spendure of a Willpower point followed by a Willpower roll (difficult 8) and a single success, what many people(including MANY of my players that love to play social characters in my chronicles &quot;since forever&quot;) complain a lot about, because according to them, it makes it &quot;trivial to resist one of the most iconic vampiric powers&quot;. Also there's the fact of whether it should work in combat or not, some argue that you cannot use it during combat, others that it only shouldn't work after you attack someone and many think you could still use Majesty and attack a target and he would be still subject to its effects somehow. Also the fact that one needs to keep spending Willpower to resist it for as long as in the presence of the cainite using Presence.<br /> <br /> Throughout my years, I've been changing one thing or two regarding its effect and use, particularly during combat, where it's more problematic. I used to rule that only Dread Gaze and Majesty were possible to be used during combat, and Majesty, only as long as the one using it doesn't attack their targets. But, then I was arguing again with a friend of mine and that made me curious to see how other ST approach Presence and its use in combat. I'd be glad to hear anything you have to tell mir about how you rule it in your games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T22:43:20-07:00","id":1543834,"title":"","content":"I would treat Presence in the way that you would treat Chimerstry. The Clanbook: Ravnos revised has a great write up about unbelief vs Chimerstry.<br /> <br /> Lets make an example. Anna is a Toreador of 9th Generation. She has Presence at 5. She walks into a parlor and turns on her Majesty attempting to make a grand entrance. While some elder Kindred would know exactly whats going on here, and would either be unaffected (lower generation) or decide to spend the willpower (aged but same generation) the majority of the viewers would be affected normally as they have no reason to suspect they're being influenced, and even if they do perhaps they don't just care in that moment.<br /> <br /> Not everyone may know that:<br /> A. She is a Toreador.<br /> B. She has Presence.<br /> C. What being influenced by it feels like.<br /> D. How to resist being influenced by it.<br /> E. That she is even using it at all.<br /> <br /> So taking the above example, perhaps she walks into the room, and instead of using her Majesty to turn heads, the player rolls Manipulation + Expression, rolls really high and makes a grand entrance just the same. Does every character there just start burning Willpower because they think they might be entranced by a Presence power? Hilariously some might because the players shouldn't know <b>what</b> is actually trying to affect them. Was it an Intimidation roll that was really high or was it Dread Gaze?<br /> <br /> I think this is a problem of meta-gaming and too much information on the players part, and not separating character knowledge from player knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T23:10:49-07:00","id":1543841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543834#post1543834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would treat Presence in the way that you would treat Chimerstry. The Clanbook: Ravnos revised has a great write up about unbelief vs Chimerstry.<br /> <br /> Lets make an example. Anna is a Toreador of 9th Generation. She has Presence at 5. She walks into a parlor and turns on her Majesty attempting to make a grand entrance. While some elder Kindred would know exactly whats going on here, and would either be unaffected (lower generation) or decide to spend the willpower (aged but same generation) the majority of the viewers would be affected normally as they have no reason to suspect they're being influenced, and even if they do perhaps they don't just care in that moment.<br /> <br /> Not everyone may know that:<br /> A. She is a Toreador.<br /> B. She has Presence.<br /> C. What being influenced by it feels like.<br /> D. How to resist being influenced by it.<br /> E. That she is even using it at all.<br /> <br /> So taking the above example, perhaps she walks into the room, and instead of using her Majesty to turn heads, the player rolls Manipulation + Expression, rolls really high and makes a grand entrance just the same. Does every character there just start burning Willpower because they think they might be entranced by a Presence power? Hilariously some might because the players shouldn't know <b>what</b> is actually trying to affect them. Was it an Intimidation roll that was really high or was it Dread Gaze?<br /> <br /> I think this is a problem of meta-gaming and too much information on the players part, and not separating character knowledge from player knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I certainly understand what you mean and I mean certainly this so called &quot;meta-gaming&quot; mentality still annoys me to this day, because even with highly experienced groups, it's still present, albeit to a much smaller degree than with new players, naturally. On the other side, I feel the need to say that the effects of Presence, especially someting like Majesty should be like &quot;a hundred times&quot; more powerful than a simple successful expression roll to impress people in a saloon. The thing is, a character should only be able to discern he's being affected by some kind of supernatural influence, if he's sucessful in a Perception + Occult roll (some might prefer to roll Awareness, instead of Occult, I think both might be valid, through different means, while Occult would give the cainite knowldge of different powers, Awareness would give himmystical sensibility to feel that &quot;something strange is happening&quot;, sometimes it might be interesting to first ask for a awareness, followed by an Occult roll to determine exactly what exactly might be at play).<br /> <br /> In any case, most people don't really resist Presence in situations like this and it's not nearly as much &quot;polemic&quot;, the &quot;controvertial&quot; applications are in more &quot;relevant scenarios&quot;, like the afore-mentioned combat situation (or any situation where there might be a risk to the unlives of the vampires).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T00:56:55-07:00","id":1543847,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543841#post1543841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other side, I feel the need to say that the effects of Presence, especially someting like Majesty should be like &quot;a hundred times&quot; more powerful than a simple successful expression roll to impress people in a saloon. .</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with Majesty in this case, I disagree with Awe, Entrancement, and Dread Gaze. Presence is supposed to be subtle, and it can't be that if so much more powerful than an exceptional roll of the applicable abilities. Now don't get me wrong I'm not talking about getting 1 success, but someone walking into the saloon with 4-5 successes on a Manipulation + Expression (or whatever traits you want to use for this) should be equivalent to using Awe in effect IMO.<br /> <br /> So I wrote up a nice long write up about each of the powers of Presence 1-5 vs combat and the forum ate it. I don't feel like doing so again, so I'll try to summarize it. I'm using the write up in the V20 VtM core as the basis.<br /> <br /> Rank 1 Awe and Rank 3 Entrancement in combat should be nulled. Awe already has a screed about self preservation, and I think that Entrancement should have had one as well as it seems like a more powerful version of Awe.<br /> <br /> Rank 4 Summon isn't really applicable since you aren't going to be doing combat versus someone you are Summoning from far away, and the effect would end when they get to you anyway. (Cast Summon to make Bob come to you so you can punch him, well once he gets there he's no longer under the effect of Summon so it doesn't matter anyway...)<br /> <br /> Rank 2 Dread Gaze (Charisma + Intimidation vs diff Courage+ Wits, a possible of 2-10 dice vs a diff of 2-10) is meant for conflict, but the victim needs to first be affected by the power to have the chance to Roll the Willpower test then spend a point, which by that point he's already lost an action. Using Ana the 9th Gen Toreador from before vs John a 13th Gen Caitiff, if she goes first she can Dread Gaze him and avoid his first attack. After he will have to either win the Willpower test and start spending Willpower to be around her, or hope she fails and botches the rolls before she can accrue enough dice to Dread Gaze him into a stupor. Dread Gaze is an extended action, and the Willpower expenditure only stops him from running away or being cowed, not losing the action dice per round.<br /> <br /> Rank 5 Majesty is also meant for conflict, but puts the onus on the victim rather than the user with the resist test. (Courage of victim vs diff of Charisma + Intimidation of the user making this is a possible 1-5 dice vs 2-10 difficulty.) Again like Dread Gaze, if the user goes first the victim will have to fail the resist test before they can even think about using Willpower, which will have to happen on the next turn because that first turn requires them to resolve the effects of Majesty first. On the second turn nothing is stopping the user of Majesty from also deciding to start using Dread Gaze as well if they go first, and once again the victim will have to resolve the effects of that. Turn three being the first turn they could reasonably use Willpower to resist, and this is if they make all the rolls, and are still in the area where this is all going down. As stated in the Majesty screed &quot;A subject who fails the roll aborts his intended action.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:34:39-07:00","id":1543872,"title":"","content":"First things first, Majesty is a social nuke. It is one of the least subtle discipline powers in the entire game, is clearly and indisputably supernatural to the point of being a potential Masquerade violation, and its use is generally considered a hostile act in and of itself. Especially in Elysia, courts, and meetings, where disciplines are nominally prohibited in sum let alone hostile discipline use. Dropping Majesty in Elysium for any reason short of immediate and necessary self-defense, or breaking up fights, is a fantastic way to make an enemy of everyone in the city, let alone the Prince, Primogen, and Sheriff whose authority you just superseded.<br /> <br /> For Toreador that's an even <i>worse</i> idea, considering to them discipline use for social events is a sign of weakness. Heads should be turning and jaws dropping because of fashion sense, swagger, entourage, and performance, not because of supernatural compulsion. Something like dropping Majesty in Elysium -- if the Toreador even survives the entirely-predictable consequences of it -- is going to get that Toreador put on the poseur list on the entire continent, if not planet, and they can kiss current or future status and clan prestige goodbye.<br /> <br /> It's not a combat-only power, but to be frank, its best use is to defuse a hostile situation <i>before</i> violence breaks out. Regardless of its use, the vampire using it absolutely should be conscious violence may break out <i>because of</i> its use, not least of all against themselves if any vampire deems necessary and prudent to attempt resisting.<br /> <br /> As far as Awe and Entrancement, there are select niche uses in conflict. Note I said &quot;conflict&quot;, not &quot;combat&quot;. For example, a scene in a Rack in which a feeding attempt goes awry, and threatens a bar fight or &quot;catch me outside&quot; scenario. Either power could be used to get a crowd's attention, influence third parties to intervene, or compel a hostile actor to instead de-escalate. Generally, once attacks start getting rolled the situation is beyond either power's capability to influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:37:50-07:00","id":1543873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543847#post1543847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While I agree with Majesty in this case, I disagree with Awe, Entrancement, and Dread Gaze. Presence is supposed to be subtle, and it can't be that if so much more powerful than an exceptional roll of the applicable abilities. Now don't get me wrong I'm not talking about getting 1 success, but someone walking into the saloon with 4-5 successes on a Manipulation + Expression (or whatever traits you want to use for this) should be equivalent to using Awe in effect IMO.<br /> <br /> So I wrote up a nice long write up about each of the powers of Presence 1-5 vs combat and the forum ate it. I don't feel like doing so again, so I'll try to summarize it. I'm using the write up in the V20 VtM core as the basis.<br /> <br /> Rank 1 Awe and Rank 3 Entrancement in combat should be nulled. Awe already has a screed about self preservation, and I think that Entrancement should have had one as well as it seems like a more powerful version of Awe.<br /> <br /> Rank 4 Summon isn't really applicable since you aren't going to be doing combat versus someone you are Summoning from far away, and the effect would end when they get to you anyway. (Cast Summon to make Bob come to you so you can punch him, well once he gets there he's no longer under the effect of Summon so it doesn't matter anyway...)<br /> <br /> Rank 2 Dread Gaze (Charisma + Intimidation vs diff Courage+ Wits, a possible of 2-10 dice vs a diff of 2-10) is meant for conflict, but the victim needs to first be affected by the power to have the chance to Roll the Willpower test then spend a point, which by that point he's already lost an action. Using Ana the 9th Gen Toreador from before vs John a 13th Gen Caitiff, if she goes first she can Dread Gaze him and avoid his first attack. After he will have to either win the Willpower test and start spending Willpower to be around her, or hope she fails and botches the rolls before she can accrue enough dice to Dread Gaze him into a stupor. Dread Gaze is an extended action, and the Willpower expenditure only stops him from running away or being cowed, not losing the action dice per round.<br /> <br /> Rank 5 Majesty is also meant for conflict, but puts the onus on the victim rather than the user with the resist test. (Courage of victim vs diff of Charisma + Intimidation of the user making this is a possible 1-5 dice vs 2-10 difficulty.) Again like Dread Gaze, if the user goes first the victim will have to fail the resist test before they can even think about using Willpower, which will have to happen on the next turn because that first turn requires them to resolve the effects of Majesty first. On the second turn nothing is stopping the user of Majesty from also deciding to start using Dread Gaze as well if they go first, and once again the victim will have to resolve the effects of that. Turn three being the first turn they could reasonably use Willpower to resist, and this is if they make all the rolls, and are still in the area where this is all going down. As stated in the Majesty screed &quot;A subject who fails the roll aborts his intended action.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good that we're on the same page regarding Majesty. I agree that Awe is/should be more subtle and as such a good charisma roll could be just as effective. Entrancement, I'd consider stronger, like &quot;a crush&quot;, but as &quot;a crush&quot;, different from &quot;Awe&quot; in some ways, it would make one more deeply fascinated by another on a deeper emotional sense, that's why I jokingly consider it to create an &quot;artificial crush&quot; on the user and its effect last longer. I'd also agree that it shouldn't be used in combat, as it would require at least a good conversation and to have someone dedicate some attention to the one using it for it to have its effect, in combat it shouldn't be possible to use it. <br /> <br /> All in all I liked your input a lot and agree with most of it. I know I sometime might appear to be someone overly worried about system and dice rolls, etc. especially considering the discussions I'm in here around the forums, but in reality I'm much more concerned about stories, I'm a writter and I love to create stories, it's by far the most important aspeect of a game, but to be able to focus much more energy on such fine stuff, I feel the need to somehow &quot;streamline&quot; these things, so that I am sure we have a balanced environment for everyone in the group to have fun in their ways. Some players like combat a lot, others avoid it like the plague, but what everyone generally agrees is that we should have a balance between different approaches to conflicts and while some might prefer to be in combat and kill their foes using martial skills, others might prefer to use a mental approach to subjulgate their enemies and others still would prefer &quot;mystical means&quot;, something we could generally and &quot;generically&quot; call &quot;magic&quot;. I like the idea that each of these players can have a system that provides them with enough balance so that all of these approaches are valid in a way, so that we can give more attention to what really matters, that is the story being told. That's why I streamline combat rules, use a lot of house rules, abolish multiple actions, etc, to try to give my players not only a more balanced environment, but one that gives room for different play styles and also we don't waste hours discussing things that shouldn't be nearly half as important as what really matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:48:33-07:00","id":1543877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543872#post1543872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First things first, Majesty is a social nuke. It is one of the least subtle discipline powers in the entire game, is clearly and indisputably supernatural to the point of being a potential Masquerade violation, and its use is generally considered a hostile act in and of itself. Especially in Elysia, courts, and meetings, where disciplines are nominally prohibited in sum let alone hostile discipline use. Dropping Majesty in Elysium for any reason short of immediate and necessary self-defense, or breaking up fights, is a fantastic way to make an enemy of everyone in the city, let alone the Prince, Primogen, and Sheriff whose authority you just superseded.<br /> <br /> For Toreador that's an even <i>worse</i> idea, considering to them discipline use for social events is a sign of weakness. Heads should be turning and jaws dropping because of fashion sense, swagger, entourage, and performance, not because of supernatural compulsion. Something like dropping Majesty in Elysium -- if the Toreador even survives the entirely-predictable consequences of it -- is going to get that Toreador put on the poseur list on the entire continent, if not planet, and they can kiss current or future status and clan prestige goodbye.<br /> <br /> It's not a combat-only power, but to be frank, its best use is to defuse a hostile situation <i>before</i> violence breaks out. Regardless of its use, the vampire using it absolutely should be conscious violence may break out <i>because of</i> its use, not least of all against themselves if any vampire deems necessary and prudent to attempt resisting.<br /> <br /> As far as Awe and Entrancement, there are select niche uses in conflict. Note I said &quot;conflict&quot;, not &quot;combat&quot;. For example, a scene in a Rack in which a feeding attempt goes awry, and threatens a bar fight or &quot;catch me outside&quot; scenario. Either power could be used to get a crowd's attention, influence third parties to intervene, or compel a hostile actor to instead de-escalate. Generally, once attacks start getting rolled the situation is beyond either power's capability to influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with everything you said, that's why I said Majesty should be &quot;a hundred times&quot; more effective than giving a good impression through a good social roll. Btw, now that you mentioned, many of my &quot;more socially inclined players&quot; (the ones who hate combat) use it exactly like you said, as a kind of last resource to avoid combat. My main question was whether or not you consider it to be used likee, after you threaten someone's (un)life, this is a hot topic and has always been in my world for more than 20 years lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T10:00:04-07:00","id":1543881,"title":"","content":"Like my old roommate said back in the 90's &quot;Presence is a combat discipline&quot;.<br /> <br /> But really, it's combat and social. <br /> <br /> Vs Mortals, Presence wins friends and favors...and sometimes stalkers. <br /> <br /> Vs Vamps and most supernatural, Presence is a WILLPOWER DRAIN. <br /> <br /> It's gonna depend upon how a ST uses the WP economy and the harder it is to replenish WP, the better Presence gets.<br /> <br /> Dread Gaze seems underwhelming at first. But I'm combat you hold your initiative until after the target spends a WP. Best used in group combat. <br /> <br /> Ally attacks target, and lands a hard shot, target really wants to parry/dodge. ST may declare or conceal if target used WP, or require a Perception roll to determine. Tricky, but it is only a level 2 power <br /> <br /> But if you are sure target greatly expended effort, the Gaze will deduct from future dice pools.<br /> <br /> Even better after Target is Grappled. <br /> <br /> Entrance is how you turn an enemies underlings against him. Great for DA campaigns and sieges. <br /> <br /> Summoning, similar to Entrance but you can get Generals/Captains out of position. Or send targets on wild chases. Etc. <br /> <br /> Majesty needs little explaining other than subject CAN expend WP and still attack the user.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T11:55:47-07:00","id":1543896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Majesty needs little explaining other than subject CAN expend WP and still attack the user. </div> </div> </div>This last sentence gave me so many heated discussions among my players over the years as a Storyteller. Many of the ones who play with more &quot;socially inclined&quot; characters used to complain that it made the power feel trivial to resist and whatnot, while the more &quot;combat inclined&quot; ones would argue that the other wants an easy &quot;I win button&quot; power, others arguing that it shoudn't work in combat or against werewolves and whatnot and so on lol. Many memories were brought back here hahaha...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T15:27:55-07:00","id":1543917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543896#post1543896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This last sentence gave me so many heated discussions among my players over the years as a Storyteller. Many of the ones who play with more &quot;socially inclined&quot; characters used to complain that it made the power feel trivial to resist and whatnot, while the more &quot;combat inclined&quot; ones would argue that the other wants an easy &quot;I win button&quot; power, others arguing that it shoudn't work in combat or against werewolves and whatnot and so on lol. Many memories were brought back here hahaha...</div> </div> </div> </div>I do want to say, after my write up, I went through editions on all the powers. 2nd edition and Revised era Presence is only resisted with a Willpower Test + Point spent for a <b>TURN</b>, and the victim has to spend another point EVERY TURN. This is huge. Most characters realistically will only have 3-5 Willpower to spend. V20 says you Willpower Test and then Point spend to resist for a <b>SCENE</b>, but offers no rules on how to keep spending points. IMO V20 is in error, because of how concentration and Willpower expenditure checks work in all editions up to V20. For example to spend Willpower to resist a derangement you are taking a whole turn to concentrate on it, and IMO this matches up with how it should work to resist the effects of Presence or any mental Discipline that allows it. In combat this is huge because it forces your victim to first fail the Power test and be affected by it (Dread Gaze forces them to flee for example, so they lose that action and must use it to flee..) then they have to use ANOTHER action/turn to concentrate and shrug off the Power itself by spending Willpower. Earlier editions like Revised were very descriptive about how this was the point where the Victim could turn around and start ignoring the user to drop the effect of the Power. I think the Revised era has the better write up for how to deal with Presence in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T16:06:18-07:00","id":1543921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543917#post1543917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do want to say, after my write up, I went through editions on all the powers. 2nd edition and Revised era Presence is only resisted with a Willpower Test + Point spent for a <b>TURN</b>, and the victim has to spend another point EVERY TURN. This is huge. Most characters realistically will only have 3-5 Willpower to spend. V20 says you Willpower Test and then Point spend to resist for a <b>SCENE</b>, but offers no rules on how to keep spending points. IMO V20 is in error, because of how concentration and Willpower expenditure checks work in all editions up to V20. For example to spend Willpower to resist a derangement you are taking a whole turn to concentrate on it, and IMO this matches up with how it should work to resist the effects of Presence or any mental Discipline that allows it. In combat this is huge because it forces your victim to first fail the Power test and be affected by it (Dread Gaze forces them to flee for example, so they lose that action and must use it to flee..) then they have to use ANOTHER action/turn to concentrate and shrug off the Power itself by spending Willpower. Earlier editions like Revised were very descriptive about how this was the point where the Victim could turn around and start ignoring the user to drop the effect of the Power. I think the Revised era has the better write up for how to deal with Presence in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>May not be in error if you factor in needing to spend WP vs multiple Majesty users in one scene. <br /> <br /> WW historically never tests/balances their games from a war gamer/competitive perspective. 'Story first' which is fair from a design standpoint, but lends itself to rule variances among tables.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T16:08:41-07:00","id":1543922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543896#post1543896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This last sentence gave me so many heated discussions among my players over the years as a Storyteller. Many of the ones who play with more &quot;socially inclined&quot; characters used to complain that it made the power feel trivial to resist and whatnot, while the more &quot;combat inclined&quot; ones would argue that the other wants an easy &quot;I win button&quot; power, others arguing that it shoudn't work in combat or against werewolves and whatnot and so on lol. Many memories were brought back here hahaha...</div> </div> </div> </div>WW was never really technically thought out or balanced with their games. <br /> <br /> It's funny how a few words between 2e and V20 can change a power. <br /> <br /> I think that's why Requiem often added generation as a means to resist powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T16:55:20-07:00","id":1543926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543921#post1543921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> May not be in error if you factor in needing to spend WP vs multiple Majesty users in one scene.<br /> <br /> WW historically never tests/balances their games from a war gamer/competitive perspective. 'Story first' which is fair from a design standpoint, but lends itself to rule variances among tables.</div> </div> </div> </div>The V20 blerb on resisting Presence is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyone can resist Presence for one scene by spending a Willpower point and succeeding on a Willpower roll (difficulty 8), but the affected individual must keep spending points until he is no longer in the presence of the vampire (or, in the case of Summon, until the effect wears off). Vampires three or more Generations lower than the wielder need only spend a single Willpower to ignore the Presence for an entire night and need not roll Willpower to do so. </div> </div> </div>The Revised edition is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyone can resist Presence for one turn by spending a Willpower point and succeeding on a Willpower roll (difficulty 8), but the affected individual must keep spending points until he can no long see the vampire (or, in the case of Summon, until the effect wears off). The simplest way to deal with this is to turn around and stop looking. Those who don't understand that they're dealing with supernatural influences (as is the case with most mortals) seldom think of this tactic, but it's a simple assumption for clever vampires. Vampires three or more generations lower than the wielder need only spend a single Willpower to ignore the Presence for an entire scene and need not roll Willpower to do so. </div> </div> </div>So the intent seems to an attempt at a direct nerf to the efficacy of the discipline but the V20 version seems incomplete with omission of the repeat expenditure timing. When does the victim spend after the first? Every turn? The next scene? If its the next scene, it kinda just invalidates the discipline entirely. So IMO with an absence of a rule, I'd default to the previous edition. So with V20 it would resist for a <i>Scene </i>as long as the victim is spending Willpower every <i>Turn</i> or until out of Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T17:29:02-07:00","id":1543934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WW was never really technically thought out or balanced with their games.<br /> <br /> It's funny how a few words between 2e and V20 can change a power. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and that balance factor is something that bother many people, myself included, as I said on another post, as a writer I'm all for story first, but for that we need to stop arguing over &quot;secondary things&quot; like the system, so I try my best to balance everything in order to allow my players to have fun playing different ways. It's similar to what I said about Koldunic sorcery being op on another post, it's clear there isn't any balance between most powers in the ST system, that's why so many adjustments are necessary. It's a good thing V5 did with celerity, multiple actions utterly break an already broken system and that's why I abolished it many years ago, there's no such a thing as multiple actions in my games, among other things. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the intent seems to an attempt at a direct nerf to the efficacy of the discipline but the V20 version seems incomplete with omission of the repeat expenditure timing. When does the victim spend after the first? Every turn? The next scene? If its the next scene, it kinda just invalidates the discipline entirely. So IMO with an absence of a rule, I'd default to the previous edition. So with V20 it would resist for a <i>Scene </i>as long as the victim is spending Willpower every <i>Turn</i> or until out of Sight.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Revised version seems to be a much better and complete one. Although we might run into a problem one of my players discussed with me many many years ago, about how Summon can bee broken if we take the RAW, because if the one resisting the power needs to spend WP for the whole duration of the power, then we have a serious problem with Summon, as not only the difficulty is low, but it's also a &quot;free power&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T18:16:28-07:00","id":1543937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543934#post1543934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, and that balance factor is something that bother many people, myself included, as I said on another post, as a writer I'm all for story first, but for that we need to stop arguing over &quot;secondary things&quot; like the system, so I try my best to balance everything in order to allow my players to have fun playing different ways. It's similar to what I said about Koldunic sorcery being op on another post, it's clear there isn't any balance between most powers in the ST system, that's why so many adjustments are necessary. It's a good thing V5 did with celerity, multiple actions utterly break an already broken system and that's why I abolished it many years ago, there's no such a thing as multiple actions in my games, among other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Revised version seems to be a much better and complete one. Although we might run into a problem one of my players discussed with me many many years ago, about how Summon can bee broken if we take the RAW, because if the one resisting the power needs to spend WP for the whole duration of the power, then we have a serious problem with Summon, as not only the difficulty is low, but it's also a &quot;free power&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm... A victim of Summon would have to spend the WP once for the Scene. Since the victim is not in the user's presence (lower case P not the discipline,) they avoid the consequence of it and the reapplication until the scene is over. The user has no way of knowing if the Summon actually worked, and the power ends at dawn automatically anyway. Unless the user has eyes on the victim some how (victim being trailed by a minion reporting back) without meta-gaming they would only get one application of Summon a night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T02:55:24-07:00","id":1543962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions#post1543830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone!<br /> So, this is a hot topic, somewhat. At least in every table I've been STing since I was a kid. How should we consider many of the functions of Presence to work, Presence is a discipline that's always bound to create some discussion about its funcioning, because on one hand anyone can resist it with a spendure of a Willpower point followed by a Willpower roll (difficult 8) and a single success, what many people(including MANY of my players that love to play social characters in my chronicles &quot;since forever&quot;) complain a lot about, because according to them, it makes it &quot;trivial to resist one of the most iconic vampiric powers&quot;. Also there's the fact of whether it should work in combat or not, some argue that you cannot use it during combat, others that it only shouldn't work after you attack someone and many think you could still use Majesty and attack a target and he would be still subject to its effects somehow. Also the fact that one needs to keep spending Willpower to resist it for as long as in the presence of the cainite using Presence.<br /> <br /> Throughout my years, I've been changing one thing or two regarding its effect and use, particularly during combat, where it's more problematic. I used to rule that only Dread Gaze and Majesty were possible to be used during combat, and Majesty, only as long as the one using it doesn't attack their targets. But, then I was arguing again with a friend of mine and that made me curious to see how other ST approach Presence and its use in combat. I'd be glad to hear anything you have to tell mir about how you rule it in your games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disclaimer: I haven't taken the time yet to read the other comments in the thread. Just sharing my own take.<br /> <br /> I mainly play VDA20 and don't remember if it's framed differently in VM20.<br /> <br /> I take Presence to be a power by which a vampire supernaturally tampers with the victim's feelings, psychically altering them or projecting a certain type of influence that will affect people around him. It does not require the vampire to do or say anything particular other than maybe make a menacing face with Dread Gaze, but I like more the idea of being perfectly poised and chilled while turning on a victim's feeling of fear towards you. Way cooler. Be as it may, I rule that it can totally be used in combat, tampering with the victim's feelings directly and immediately.<br /> <br /> As for the roll to resist, I house rule that the number of successes is taken from the successes rolled by the vampire, not that a single success suffices to resist. The alternative just doesn't appeal to me at all.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T16:35:32-07:00","id":1544033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543962#post1543962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Disclaimer: I haven't taken the time yet to read the other comments in the thread. Just sharing my own take.<br /> <br /> I mainly play VDA20 and don't remember if it's framed differently in VM20.<br /> <br /> I take Presence to be a power by which a vampire supernaturally tampers with the victim's feelings, psychically altering them or projecting a certain type of influence that will affect people around him. It does not require the vampire to do or say anything particular other than maybe make a menacing face with Dread Gaze, but I like more the idea of being perfectly poised and chilled while turning on a victim's feeling of fear towards you. Way cooler. Be as it may, I rule that it can totally be used in combat, tampering with the victim's feelings directly and immediately.<br /> <br /> As for the roll to resist, I house rule that the number of successes is taken from the successes rolled by the vampire, not that a single success suffices to resist. The alternative just doesn't appeal to me at all.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe this way it gets too op, especially considering the limitations of Willpower dicepool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T17:29:25-07:00","id":1544038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1544033#post1544033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe this way it gets too op, especially considering the limitations of Willpower dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point for me is that on average it should work.<br /> <br /> Let's look at Dread Gaze: its main benefit is reaped in the same scene and turn it is used, for example saving a social vampire from a physical confrontation. It targets one opponent at a time, so it does not help a lot when facing multiple opponents (a standard, not supernaturally powered, Intimidation roll might help more there - see below). If the opponent can resist for the turn or scene by spending a Willpower point and scoring a single success on difficulty 8, on average anyone with Willpower 5+ will succeed and attack the vampire for the turn, regardless of the vampire's trait ratings. Next turn the vampire might suffer from wound penalties, making things even harder. <br /> <br /> By contrast, the rules for social rolls are somewhat undefined, and in VDA20 there isn't even an explanation of how to physically intimidate a group rather than a single individual, which I consider a standard, common thing to try to do to avoid a fight, like when trying to scare off a gang, but the normal Intimidation roll 1 on 1 is Strength/Manipulation + Intimidate on diff.6 vs Willpower or Strength+Intimidate on the same difficulty. This means that, 1 against 1, a vampire will see his dice pool and traits count here more than on the Dread Gaze roll, and if it's a Strength roll he can even bear blood expenditure and Potence to bear. In VDA20, when trying to scare off multiple opponents, one could apply the modifier for fighting multiple opponents (+1 per enemy after the first, max +4), making things harder but possible, especially if one has automatic successes from Potence. The result is that, unless there are other factors and modifiers at play. In many cases mundane intimidation attempts have more chances of succeeding - especially for Potence weilders - than Dread Gaze.<br /> <br /> Sure, Dread Gaze might be active for multiple turns and force the victim to continue spending Willpower points until they leave the vampire's presence, but that's hardly relevant because often you really need it to work in the first turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T18:17:58-07:00","id":1544046,"title":"","content":"In general, the main problem with evaluating Presence and other socially-oriented Disciplines is that, while social actions should be central to the game (VtM is supposed to be more socially oriented than other game lines, since vampires are squashed physically by werewolves and I guess mentally by mages - whatever that means), the game system is underwhelming when it comes to defining social rolls and mechanics.<br /> <br /> Sure, that works if your playstyle is purely narrative, but then social Disciplines should be narrative, too. If you prefer a game where you can have a reliable system to compare the characters' capaciites and avoid dispute at the table, VtM's mechanics are too vague for mundane rolls and that spills into the comparison between using Disciplines and using mundane rolls, which then makes one question the usefulness of social disciplines and therefore the one thing vampires are supposed to be good at in the setting compared to other supernaturals. My VDA20 group (where I was a player, not ST) reached a near consensus that making social characters and investing in social traits and Disciplines other than Dominate was a waste of dots and experience... Sure, that has a lot to do with how the ST handled things, but it's a problematic outcome for a group that has been playing various editions of VtM and VDA for years.<br /> <br /> In Chronicles of Darkness there is a good alternative, in my opinion, because social rolls are better structured and many supernatural powers to influence others are framed as clear and sensible advantages to the factors in social rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T21:49:36-07:00","id":1544073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> since vampires are squashed physically by werewolves and I guess mentally by mages </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't really know what kind of games you've been playing lol, but anyway, vampire games tend to bee more social than werewolf or mage, but that's just that, a tendency, not a rule. The whole &quot;Vampion&quot; trend the past already shows us that the game can be quite different, also when we have Dark Ages, an arguably more combat oriented setting, things can differ a lot. As I always say, the game is what the Storyteller and his group want it to be, some groups are more social, but even in those there are normally a few combats, etc. also even on a &quot;Full Vampion&quot; game, there might be a lot of social scenes and chapters, etc. again, the nature of the game is going to depend a lot on what the group want, there's no rule. From my observation, funny enough, social games tend to be the more present at one-shot stories normally found at events and the likes (especially live action events, naturally and so on), but &quot;Vampion&quot; tables tend to last longer, ofc this is my observation taken from my experience, but even in my experience it tends to vary a lot and I've seen A LOT of games over my 20+ experience, mostly as a Storyteller, but I also watched many of my friend's games and they would often invite me to play an antagonist on their stories, because since I was very young I was known for my taste for intense roleplaying and my friends liked to bring that to their tables sometimes (I even studied acting for a while when I was about 13-16).<br /> <br /> Anyway, the thing is however our &quot;approach&quot; is, that is, the game style, be it more investigative, more social or more combat oriented, we need balance, however problematic the Storyteller System is, we can try to find balance in it in order to allow everyone to have fun and focus on what really matter, the story. For that I feel it's very helpful to have a stable and balanced system, so I think here in this example we're talking on this thread, perhaps a small buff compared to V20, making the resistance last 1 turn, instead of a scene, could be nice, but to ask for people to have more success on a WP roll, that they already spent WP to even attempt in the first place and that also has a target number of 8, is too much. I'm sure that 9 out of 10 storytellers would agree that it would make Presence borderline broken (but still not as broken as RAW celerity, probably the most broken thing in the entire line lol).<br /> <br /> Tbh, the thing I really wanted opinion here is if it makes sense to be able to use Majesty after you attack someone, for instance, during a combat where you have already threatened someone's existence and then use Majesty and whether it should have an effect or not. This is probably the most polemic situation regarding Presence use in my experience and I'm still in doubt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 10-17-2024, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T04:47:51-07:00","id":1544087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1544073#post1544073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I don't really know what kind of games you've been playing lol, but anyway, vampire games tend to bee more social than werewolf or mage, but that's just that, a tendency, not a rule. The whole &quot;Vampion&quot; trend the past already shows us that the game can be quite different, also when we have Dark Ages, an arguably more combat oriented setting, things can differ a lot. As I always say, the game is what the Storyteller and his group want it to be, some groups are more social, but even in those there are normally a few combats, etc. also even on a &quot;Full Vampion&quot; game, there might be a lot of social scenes and chapters, etc. again, the nature of the game is going to depend a lot on what the group want, there's no rule. From my observation, funny enough, social games tend to be the more present at one-shot stories normally found at events and the likes (especially live action events, naturally and so on), but &quot;Vampion&quot; tables tend to last longer, ofc this is my observation taken from my experience, but even in my experience it tends to vary a lot and I've seen A LOT of games over my 20+ experience, mostly as a Storyteller, but I also watched many of my friend's games and they would often invite me to play an antagonist on their stories, because since I was very young I was known for my taste for intense roleplaying and my friends liked to bring that to their tables sometimes (I even studied acting for a while when I was about 13-16).<br /> <br /> Anyway, the thing is however our &quot;approach&quot; is, that is, the game style, be it more investigative, more social or more combat oriented, we need balance, however problematic the Storyteller System is, we can try to find balance in it in order to allow everyone to have fun and focus on what really matter, the story. For that I feel it's very helpful to have a stable and balanced system, so I think here in this example we're talking on this thread, perhaps a small buff compared to V20, making the resistance last 1 turn, instead of a scene, could be nice, but to ask for people to have more success on a WP roll, that they already spent WP to even attempt in the first place and that also has a target number of 8, is too much. I'm sure that 9 out of 10 storytellers would agree that it would make Presence borderline broken (but still not as broken as RAW celerity, probably the most broken thing in the entire line lol).<br /> <br /> Tbh, the thing I really wanted opinion here is if it makes sense to be able to use Majesty after you attack someone, for instance, during a combat where you have already threatened someone's existence and then use Majesty and whether it should have an effect or not. This is probably the most polemic situation regarding Presence use in my experience and I'm still in doubt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on the need for a balanced system.<br /> I sort of disagree on the idea that requiring more successes is broken, but I see your point. Lowering the difficulty wouldn't do much though because then it becomes too similar to how mundane social rolls work, in my opinion. We'll just agree to disagree on it being broken or not.<br /> <br /> As for Majesty, I don't understand the issue very well. I don't see why having attacked someone already or having been attacked by them should come in Majesty's way, unless you attacked them and rolled multiple 1s and no success, at which point you might have embarrassed yourself too much to be taken seriously.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T14:47:51-07:00","id":1544359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1543934#post1543934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, and that balance factor is something that bother many people, myself included, as I said on another post, as a writer I'm all for story first, but for that we need to stop arguing over &quot;secondary things&quot; like the system, so I try my best to balance everything in order to allow my players to have fun playing different ways. It's similar to what I said about Koldunic sorcery being op on another post, it's clear there isn't any balance between most powers in the ST system, that's why so many adjustments are necessary. It's a good thing V5 did with celerity, multiple actions utterly break an already broken system and that's why I abolished it many years ago, there's no such a thing as multiple actions in my games, among other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Revised version seems to be a much better and complete one. Although we might run into a problem one of my players discussed with me many many years ago, about how Summon can bee broken if we take the RAW, because if the one resisting the power needs to spend WP for the whole duration of the power, then we have a serious problem with Summon, as not only the difficulty is low, but it's also a &quot;free power&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>True<br /> <br /> WW's lack of balance doesnt bother me...<i>any more</i>.<br /> <br /> Ive come to the conclusion that even WW admits each table should use it as they see fit and the main backbone needed to carry the system is consistency between ST and Players in upholding any homebrew fixes or interpretations. <br /> <br /> Im fully confident that i can patch any issues were i to be the ST in a way that is consistent and fun for the Players. The mechanics are just a conveyance for a shared experience. I i want super tight rules like wargaming, i can do that. If i want diceless freeform, i can do that as well. ST System is more fluid than people realize. Its comes down to how do you want Realism to factor in as well as how much randomness do you want there to be in the Actions.<br /> <br /> Koldunism OP? Obtenebration2/3 OP? Majesty OP? <br /> <br /> People can quibble, as is their right in these endeavors, on which levels need nerfed/buffed/etc. But the framework is there - the powers are levelled in ascending leverage and ability do the simple logic is to fit them into that scale. Majesty, lvl5 should be powerful. Shroud of Night lvl2 likely should NOT have all those maluses and alter the environment so much. The system isnt balanced per se, but there is a framework for proportion that can be referenced.<br /> <br /> Summon can be used tactically in combat or over a night, or can be more of a plot device. PC Summons NPC and ST has to roll or otherwise adjudicate if NPC reaches destination in a reasonable time, usually a deadline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T10:04:28-07:00","id":1544570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543830-on-the-premise-of-how-presence-functions?p=1544359#post1544359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True<br /> <br /> WW's lack of balance doesnt bother me...<i>any more</i>.<br /> <br /> Ive come to the conclusion that even WW admits each table should use it as they see fit and the main backbone needed to carry the system is consistency between ST and Players in upholding any homebrew fixes or interpretations.<br /> <br /> Im fully confident that i can patch any issues were i to be the ST in a way that is consistent and fun for the Players. The mechanics are just a conveyance for a shared experience. I i want super tight rules like wargaming, i can do that. If i want diceless freeform, i can do that as well. ST System is more fluid than people realize. Its comes down to how do you want Realism to factor in as well as how much randomness do you want there to be in the Actions.<br /> <br /> Koldunism OP? Obtenebration2/3 OP? Majesty OP?<br /> <br /> People can quibble, as is their right in these endeavors, on which levels need nerfed/buffed/etc. But the framework is there - the powers are levelled in ascending leverage and ability do the simple logic is to fit them into that scale. Majesty, lvl5 should be powerful. Shroud of Night lvl2 likely should NOT have all those maluses and alter the environment so much. The system isnt balanced per se, but there is a framework for proportion that can be referenced.<br /> <br /> Summon can be used tactically in combat or over a night, or can be more of a plot device. PC Summons NPC and ST has to roll or otherwise adjudicate if NPC reaches destination in a reasonable time, usually a deadline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely, the system is imbalanced, but it's quite simple to fix those things. Even more so given how emphasized the &quot;Golden Rule&quot; in the WoD line, I mean I guess every ST with some experience has at some point run into the (in)famous &quot;rules lawyer&quot;, but if I see something I consider imbalanced or unfair I just straight say &quot;no, wee need to fix this power&quot; and often do that in the middle of a game session if relevant and later create a new set of rules for any &quot;problematic power&quot;, like the (in)famous Paws of the Newborn Cub that when storytelling cross-overs as there are unfortunately a small number of werewolf players who like the idea of using a &quot;one win button&quot; against another splat, I just say, &quot;not really, we need a resisted roll here, you're not going to make our colleague here playing an interesting and powerful mage just becomes powerless for some turns because someone at WW didn't have any idea of how to properly develop rules for this power and instead decided to go 'whatever, nobody is going to use it anyway, make it a one-win button lame power', your colleague deserves to have fun as well in a balanced envinroment&quot; and similar situations, <br /> <br /> So yes, overall, while it is problematic, it's not really hard for an experienced ST to solve this problems and that's why I stick to the system, despite its flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T18:20:30-07:00","id":1544696,"title":"","content":"Ah, how I loved to use the Presence with my Setite... I played a game upon we were all 4th gen raised in Enoch. Obfuscation 9, then Serpentis 1 (paralizes the target, no resist possible), then I would just simply do whatever I wanted with my target... Like a snake playing with a mice... I once used that combo to teach a lesson to the Gangrels at their own moot (my best friend was a 4th gen Gangrel). I said &quot;oh, let's duel, but take it easy cuz I'm not a warrior&quot;, then poof, vanished under a three only to paralize my target and play with him with Presence 3. Paralized, there's no limit to how long I can do it, until he was left in shambles. I did this to remember the Gangrels at the moot that their adversaries would not be honourable (I was a good Setite, I became a student and foster child of Saulot and then I converted to Osirism... It was a crazy table, don't ask. I even reached Golconda. Yeah, like I said, crazy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}